# Sleeper Data Model

- Treat Sleeper as the source of truth for leagues, rosters, drafts, picks, transactions, matchups, player identity, team, depth-chart metadata, and NFL state.
- Normalize raw Sleeper responses at the provider boundary before passing data into modules.
- Keep domain types provider-neutral, even when current data comes from Sleeper.
- Do not assume the `players/nfl` response includes `bye_week`; current bye-week values may be schedule-derived.
- Use `src/providers/schedule/nflScheduleApi.ts` to enrich missing player bye weeks by team.
- Keep external schedule enrichment isolated from Sleeper normalization so fallback/enrichment behavior remains easy to reason about.
